{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs",
  "item": "impl[CachedProvider/SourceProvider]/fn[read]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The provider overrides parse with a cached snapshot. Selected-source\n reads must deliver and fingerprint that snapshot without fetching again;\n this trait-required callback rejects a refetch. Primitive provider reads\n are covered separately, and executing this guard would fail this test."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#impl[CachedProvider/SourceProvider]/fn[read]` is justified.\n\n- **Form:** it is an explicit function with a body, and its fenced commentary gives the reason.\n- **Substance:** the reason is not just difficulty. The sibling `fn[parse]` overrides parsing and returns a fixed cached snapshot, `fn observed() { call(); }`, through `parse_snapshot`. `fn[read]` only returns `Err(SourceError::Invalid(\"must not refetch\"))`, so it is a guard against refetching.\n- **Agreement with the test:** `cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input` expects the delivered snapshot's content as the fingerprint value. A refetch would break that, so running `read` would fail the test. That matches the commentary's claim that executing the guard would fail the test.\n- **Trait requirement:** `fn[read]` is required by the `SourceProvider` trait, as the commentary says.\n\nThe commentary agrees with the current source, and the exception is acceptable.",
